    "narrative": "The offensive core for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the high-upside speed dynamics of **Corbin Carroll** (81.94) and **Mickey Moniak** (72.05). **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Rocker and an elite speed environment created by a slow delivery, which significantly boosts his SB potential. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime spot; his aggressive dynamic platoon advantage against Keller is the primary driver behind his strong score, providing a critical boost in a category where we cannot afford to fall behind. **Josh Naylor** (74.98) serves as the anchor of the lineup, leveraging a massive +19% boost from the SP skill gap against McCullers Jr. to solidify our run production potential.\n\nWhile **James Wood** (66.07) provides excellent value at the leadoff spot, our decision-making regarding the bottom of the order remains tight. **Kyle Karros** (46.81) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, narrowly missing the cut behind **Cole Young**. While **Kyle Karros** possesses a solid analytical profile, the optimizer favored **Cole Young** due to the latter's proximity to a high-SB-conducive matchup, even despite the drop-off in batting order position. Meanwhile, **Zach McKinstry** (40.20) sits right on our efficiency floor; his start is contingent on his ability to navigate the park factors and Scott\u2019s peripherals, as he remains our most volatile asset today.\n\nWe must monitor the health status of our depth chart, as **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Jose Caballero** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our ability to rotate for defensive or platoon upgrades. Risks are concentrated in the middle of the order where **Austin Riley** faces a formidable arm in Imanaga, whose ability to limit extra-base hits slightly caps our ceiling in the HR category. We are heavily invested in exploiting the 5x5 scarcity of stolen bases today, and any defensive adjustments from the opposing managers\u2014specifically catcher pop times\u2014could dampen the anticipated output of our aggressive baserunners like **Brice Turang** and **Trevor Story**.",
